---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Intro from "../components/Intro.astro";
import SeasonCards from "../components/SeasonCards.astro";
import OfferOverview from "../components/OfferOverview.astro";
import GalleryShow from "../components/GalleryShow.astro";
import Compositions from "../components/Compositions.astro";
import FacebookNews from "../components/FacebookNews.astro";
import Directions from "../components/Directions.astro";
import { homeGallery } from "../data/gallery";

/**
 * The home page: what the holding sells, which part of the year is running, what it looks
 * like, and how to get there.
 *
 * ## Where the photo show sits, and why there
 *
 * `GalleryShow` stands between the offer tiles and the plantings: the tiles say what is sold,
 * the show says what it looks like, and only then come the plantings, which are a different
 * question again. It is also the only place it can go. The sections alternate light and dark,
 * two dark plates cannot be told apart from each other (--green-band in tokens.css), and there
 * were no two adjacent light sections to put a dark one between - so the new band is light, and
 * a light band next to `--paper-clay` is the arrangement the top of this page already uses
 * three times over.
 *
 * It carries **69 photographs** - every frame of the offer that is the holding's own and is
 * not already on this page - one row at a time. That is not 69 photographs' worth of page:
 * `gallery-show.ts` mounts three rows and hides the rest, and a hidden image is never
 * fetched. The "Więcej zdjęć" row under it points at `#zdjecia` on each category page,
 * which is the strip that holds that group's full set.
 *
 * It used to be the entire site - fourteen plant descriptions, the gallery, the history and
 * the contact section on one scroll, with a menu whose five entries pointed at three
 * anchors. Cutting it back to an intro, the season and four tiles then went too far the
 * other way: the holding has 48 photographs of its own, that entrance showed four of them,
 * and the offer tiles carried none at all - on a business whose whole product is what a
 * plant looks like.
 *
 * **So this page shows the pictures, and only the pictures.** It is a preview of each part
 * of the site rather than a table of contents for it - but a preview, not a copy. The
 * subpages keep what makes them worth opening: the cultivation descriptions, the colour
 * lists, the filters, the phone numbers.
 *
 * Outline: `h1` in Intro, then one `h2` per section.
 *
 * ## The two blocks that repeat something, and what earns them their place
 *
 * - **Inspiracje** shows the same 23 plantings as `/inspiracje/`, with the filter, the
 *   thumbnail rail, the anchors, the structured data and the per-panel phone CTA all
 *   switched off (see the props on `Compositions.astro`). Every panel heading is a link to
 *   that planting on `/inspiracje/`, so the preview feeds the page rather than replacing it.
 * - **Directions** stands where `ContactStrip` stood in 0.5, and would deserve the same
 *   deletion if it repeated what that one did. It does not: it prints no phone number.
 *   The strip was removed because `602 518 401` appeared three times on this page - in the
 *   Intro call button, in the strip and in the footer. The block answers the one question
 *   the footer cannot: where this is, on a map.
 *
 * **The phone count is the thing to watch on this page, and it is easy to get wrong.** The
 * first draft of 0.7 shipped the plantings strip with its panel CTA intact and put the number
 * on this page **25 times** - once in the Intro, once in the footer and once in each of the
 * 23 panels - while this very comment claimed it appeared once. Anything repeated per panel
 * is repeated 23 times here. Count it on the built page before trusting a sentence about it:
 * `grep -o 'href="tel:' dist/index.html | wc -l` should read **3**: the intro's one CTA plus the
 * footer's list of both numbers. The check used to name a number - `602 518 401` - which
 * stopped existing when the owners withdrew two of the four phones, so it was passing by
 * matching nothing. Count the links, not a particular number.
 *
 * ## The block that is not a preview of anything
 *
 * **Aktualności** (`FacebookNews`) stands between the plantings and the map, and it is the one
 * thing on this page that has no subpage behind it. The catalogue changes once a season; this
 * is where "chryzantemy są już w sprzedaży" can appear on a Tuesday, because the owners write
 * it on Facebook and a workflow carries it here.
 *
 * **It is now load-bearing, which it was not before.** Until September 2026 this block vanished
 * when the snapshot was empty and the page had to read correctly without it. Since the home
 * page went to alternating grounds it is the light band between the plantings plate and the
 * directions plate, and two dark plates cannot be told apart from each other (--green-band in
 * tokens.css explains why the usable range is that narrow). So the block renders whether or not
 * there are posts, and moving it, or letting it disappear again, merges two sections into one.
 *
 * The map is consent-gated, and the Facebook block needs no gate because it embeds nothing -
 * its pictures are our own files. So the home page still contacts nothing but our own server
 * until a visitor asks for the map.
 */

const galleryGroups = await homeGallery();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Gospodarstwo Ogrodnicze „Saran” - kwiaty balkonowe, rabatowe i chryzantemy"
  description="Rodzinne gospodarstwo w Cholewiance pod Kazimierzem Dolnym. Kwiaty balkonowe, rabatowe i wieloletnie oraz chryzantemy wielkokwiatowe z własnej uprawy. Zamówienia telefonicznie lub na miejscu."
  canonical="/"
>
  <Intro />
  <SeasonCards />
  <OfferOverview />
  <GalleryShow groups={galleryGroups} />
  <Compositions
    level={2}
    showFilters={false}
    showRail={false}
    structuredData={false}
    ids={false}
    prose={false}
    allLink
    ground="dark"
  />
  <FacebookNews />
  <Directions />
</BaseLayout>
